00:23:33.000 --> 00:24:10.000
flip a coin and say it's Mexican. today, it's not going to be French. So it turns out flipping a coin is actually an optimal strategy under some circumstances. So that's a good way of solving the explorer exploit tradeoff where you, you know, some of the time are willing to flip a coin. The only thing that I would say is that the rate at which you flip a coin should be decreasing over time. So the longer you stay in a city, you should be taking that random action with lower probability. And then that turns out to be an optimal algorithm too. Well, let's talk about one really big picture question.

